PARITY MAPPING (web → Apple platform tokens; no Tailwind ported, no raw hex, no English literals)
  border glass-border / bg surface-1 / text-primary  → Color.TS.border / .surface / .textPrimary
  placeholder text-muted                             → SwiftUI prompt (muted by default) + leading icon Color.TS.textMuted
  error border-red-500 / error <p>                   → Color.TS.statusDanger (border) / InputMessageText(.error)
  hint text-muted <p>                                → Color.TS.textMuted via InputMessageText(.hint)
  focus:ring-2 ring-blue-500                          → @FocusState ⇒ 2pt Color.TS.accent ring overlay (coexists w/ error border)
  disabled:opacity-50                                → .opacity(0.5).disabled(true)
  Label text-sm font-medium text-secondary           → Font.TS.body.weight(.medium) + Color.TS.textSecondary
  required `*` + sr-only word                        → statusDanger glyph (.accessibilityHidden) + folded into field a11y name
  <HelpIcon>                                          → InputHelpButton ("(?)" SF Symbol) + popover + .help() tooltip
  sizeClasses sm/md/lg/auto                           → InputMetrics 8/6·12 · 12/8·14 · 16/10·16 · md baseline (Dynamic Type)
  i18n   : label/error/hint/prompt are caller LocalizedStringKeys; only native chrome owns keys (P1/S10 facade)
  a11y   : field named after label (+required word) — the htmlFor linkage; error/hint as accessibilityHint
           (aria-describedby); help button per-field label "Help for {field}"; reduce-motion-gated focus animation;
           Dynamic Type via Font.system(size:); container .accessibilityElement(children:.contain)
  telemetry : view.opened surface="Input" via InputSurface.reportOpen (P1/S11), default OSLog sink.

